  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Sustainable Reintegration for Iraqi Nationals Returning from Abroad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project will contribute to the sustainable reintegration of Iraqis returning from abroad through voluntary and non-voluntary returns. To achieve this, IOM would like to propose the following: a) implement community-based reintegration projects to support Iraqi returnees and community members in achieving sustainable reintegration in areas of high return and potential migration that will be implemented using a participatory approach involving returnees and their communities of return to address wider needs and concerns; b) provision of specialized protection, MHPSS and economic reintegration services to Iraqi returnees according to pre-identified vulnerability criteria and following referrals from the GoI; and c) consultations with the GoI and non-government stakeholders including the private sector, on strengthening reintegration services and their impact for Iraqi returnees.</narrative>
  </description>
